#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1564
msgid "Gym plates in metric gyms are often 1.25, 2.5, 5, 10, 15, and 20 kg. US customary gyms use 2.5, 5, 10, 25, 35, and 45 lb plates. A “20 kg plate” is about 44.1 lb—not a 45 lb plate. When following a program written in the other system, convert working weights, then choose the nearest plate combination and log what you actually lifted."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2168
msgid "Gym programs written in pounds need working weights in pounds. Convert body weight only if the program indexes loads to body weight; otherwise convert the prescribed plate weights, not your nickname weight in stone."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2459
msgid "Gym treadmills may default to mph in the US and km/h elsewhere. Hitting “10” intending 10 km/h on an mph treadmill is an all-out sprint (~16 km/h). Check the unit indicator every time you start a belt on travel."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:463
msgid "Habits for error-free prefix conversion"
msgstr "Kebiasaan untuk konversi awalan bebas kesalahan"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2184
msgid "Half-stone changes (7 lb ≈ 3.2 kg) are common in fitness talk. Convert the change the same way you convert absolute weight."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:310
msgid "Halving the pound value (“close enough to kg”) is ~10% low. Baby weight in pounds and ounces needs ounces converted (16 oz = 1 lb) before switching to kg. Do not use troy or tower pounds here."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1076
msgid "Hard conversion uses exact factors and preserves the original intent as closely as rounding allows. Soft conversion chooses a convenient near value in the other unit system, possibly adjusting tolerances, for manufacturability in local tooling."
msgstr "Konversi keras menggunakan faktor eksak dan mempertahankan maksud awal sedekat mungkin dengan pembulatan. Konversi lunak memilih nilai mendekati yang sesuai dalam sistem unit lain, mungkin menyesuaikan toleransi, untuk kemampuan manufaktur dalam perkakas lokal."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1028
msgid "Hard conversion uses exact factors and then rounds according to a stated rule that preserves the intent of the tolerance. Soft conversion picks a convenient nearby nominal in the other system. Both are valid strategies—but they are different strategies. Write which one you used in the revision block."
msgstr "Konversi keras menggunakan faktor eksak dan kemudian membulatkannya sesuai dengan aturan yang ditetapkan yang mempertahankan maksud dari toleransi. Konversi lunak memilih nominal terdekat yang sesuai di sistem lain. Keduanya adalah strategi yang valid—tetapi keduanya merupakan strategi yang berbeda. Tulis yang mana yang Anda gunakan di blok revisi."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:236
msgid "Hardware acceleration and GPU pipelines often force floats. In those cases, keep authoritative conversion in decimal on the CPU or server, and treat GPU floats as a display or intermediate approximation."
msgstr "Akselerasi perangkat keras dan pipeline GPU sering kali memaksa float. Dalam kasus tersebut, pertahankan konversi otoritatif dalam desimal pada CPU atau server, dan perlakukan GPU float sebagai tampilan atau perkiraan perantara."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2484
msgid "Heart-rate or power targets are independent of unit labels, but the treadmill prescription you programmed is not. Log the unit you actually used."
msgstr ""

