#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:900
msgid "William Thomson (Lord Kelvin) advanced absolute thermodynamic temperature. The kelvin starts at absolute zero and uses the same degree size as Celsius. Equations of gas behaviour and statistical mechanics prefer absolute scales because ratios and absolute values behave cleanly without arbitrary offsets."
msgstr "William Thomson (Lord Kelvin) memajukan suhu termodinamika absolut. Kelvin dimulai dari nol mutlak dan menggunakan ukuran derajat yang sama dengan Celcius. Persamaan perilaku gas dan mekanika statistik lebih memilih skala absolut karena rasio dan nilai absolut berperilaku bersih tanpa offset yang berubah-ubah."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1785
msgid "Wind reports in marine forecasts often use knots. A “20-knot wind” is about 37 km/h or 23 mph. Small-craft advice thresholds are written in knots in many countries; convert only after you understand the category boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2248
msgid "Wind shear of the mental kind"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2311
msgid "Work shifts logged as “7.5 hours” are durations. Convert to minutes (450) for payroll systems that want minutes. Time-zone entry only matters for when the shift started, not for how long 7.5 hours is."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1881
msgid "Worked conversion patterns"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/conversion-details.tsx:191
msgid "Worked example"
msgstr "Contoh pengerjaan"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:161
msgid "Worked habit for area: 200 ft² to m². First convert length: 1 ft = 0.3048 m, so 1 ft² = 0.092 903 04 m². Then 200 × 0.092 903 04 = 18.580 608 m². Notice the squared factor—skipping that step would be catastrophically wrong."
msgstr "Kebiasaan bekerja untuk area: 200 ft² hingga m². Panjang konversi pertama: 1 kaki = 0,3048 m, jadi 1 kaki² = 0,092 903 04 m². Maka 200 × 0,092 903 04 = 18,580 608 m². Perhatikan faktor kuadratnya—melewatkan langkah itu adalah kesalahan besar."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:160
msgid "Worked habit: convert 12 ft to metres. Use 1 ft (international) = 0.3048 m exactly. 12 × 0.3048 = 3.6576 m. For display you might write 3.658 m or 3.66 m depending on tolerance."
msgstr "Kebiasaan bekerja: ubah 12 kaki menjadi meter. Gunakan tepat 1 kaki (internasional) = 0,3048 m. 12 × 0,3048 = 3,6576 m. Untuk tampilan Anda dapat menulis 3,658 m atau 3,66 m tergantung toleransi."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2398
msgid "Worked patterns"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1735
msgid "Workflow for a border-crossing day"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:839
msgid "Workflow for trustworthy land conversions"
msgstr "Alur kerja untuk konversi lahan yang dapat dipercaya"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2189
msgid "Workflow worth repeating"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1395
msgid "Write both °C and °F on a sticky note for family recipes you reuse. Dual labels prevent weekend arguments and burnt trays."
msgstr "Tuliskan °C dan °F pada catatan tempel untuk resep keluarga yang Anda gunakan kembali. Label ganda mencegah pertengkaran di akhir pekan dan baki terbakar."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:607
msgid "Write m² and m³ with clear superscripts or ASCII m^2 and m^3 in plain text. A bare m next to a number that meant cubic metres will be misread later."
msgstr "Tulis m² dan m³ dengan superskrip yang jelas atau ASCII m^2 dan m^3 dalam teks biasa. Tanda m di sebelah angka yang berarti meter kubik nantinya akan salah dibaca."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1335
msgid "Write the unit on every sketch dimension. A bare “12 × 15” is ambiguous across borders. Prefer “12 ft × 15 ft” or “3.66 m × 4.57 m”."
msgstr "Tuliskan satuan pada setiap dimensi sketsa. Angka “12 × 15” yang kosong bersifat ambigu antar negara. Lebih suka “12 kaki × 15 kaki” atau “3,66 m × 4,57 m”."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:466
msgid "Write units on every line of a calculation. Prefix errors hide in bare numbers. Dimensional analysis still works when prefixes are treated as part of the unit token."
msgstr "Tuliskan satuan pada setiap baris perhitungan. Kesalahan awalan disembunyikan dalam angka kosong. Analisis dimensi masih berfungsi ketika prefiks diperlakukan sebagai bagian dari token unit."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2003
msgid "Write units on the sketch: “3.20 m × 4.10 m” or “10 ft 6 in × 13 ft 5 in.” Bare numbers cause expensive callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:248
msgid "Writing “mL” on a value still in litres by habit (1 L ≠ 1 mL). Baby formula and concentrate ratios break if you convert volume but keep the powder mass wrong. Carbonated beverage “litres” on bottles are liquid volume, not dissolved-gas volume."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:358
msgid "Writing 1.5 kg as 1.5 g on a scale that reads grams underdoses by 1,000×. Shipping dimensional weight in kg is unrelated to converting product mass to grams—keep those workflows separate. Jewelry grams are mass; carats are different."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:458
msgid "Writing 90 minutes as 1.90 hours is wrong—90/60 = 1.5 h. Movie runtimes in minutes convert cleanly; including trailers is a content choice, not a unit issue. Keep overtime rules (e.g. round to next 15 min) separate from pure conversion."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:1228
msgid "Yard (International)"
msgstr "Halaman (Internasional)"

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:401
msgid "Year (Julian)"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:858
msgid "Yes—both are area units. One square kilometre equals 100 hectares, or about 247.1 acres. Converting through square metres or hectares keeps the arithmetic clear."
msgstr "Ya—keduanya merupakan satuan luas. Satu kilometer persegi sama dengan 100 hektar, atau sekitar 247,1 hektar. Mengonversi melalui meter persegi atau hektar membuat perhitungannya tetap jelas."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1470
msgid "Yes—distance and speed share the same length unit in km/h vs mph. Convert carefully; small mistakes matter at highway speeds."
msgstr "Ya—jarak dan kecepatan memiliki satuan panjang yang sama dalam km/jam vs mph. Konversikan dengan hati-hati; kesalahan kecil penting pada kecepatan jalan raya."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:319
msgid "Yes. Absolute zero is 0 K, which equals −273.15 °C. No ordinary thermodynamic system reaches temperatures below that value."
msgstr "Ya. Nol mutlak adalah 0 K, yang sama dengan −273,15 °C. Tidak ada sistem termodinamika biasa yang mencapai suhu di bawah nilai tersebut."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:553
msgid "Yes. One metre is about 1.094 yards, or roughly 3.281 feet. A metre is a little longer than a yard."
msgstr "Ya. Satu meter sama dengan 1.094 yard, atau kira-kira 3.281 kaki. Satu meter sedikit lebih panjang dari satu yard."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1155
msgid "Yes. One micrometre equals 1 000 nanometres. Both equal 10⁻⁶ m and 10⁻⁹ m × 1 000 respectively."
msgstr "Ya. Satu mikrometer sama dengan 1.000 nanometer. Keduanya sama dengan 10⁻⁶ m dan 10⁻⁹ m × 1.000."

#: src/routes/$lang/convert.$quantity.$from.to.$to.tsx:92
msgid "Yes. Units Converters is free to use for students, professionals, and everyday tasks. Results are for informational purposes."
msgstr "Ya. Units Converters gratis digunakan untuk pelajar, profesional, dan tugas sehari-hari. Hasil adalah untuk tujuan informasi."

#: src/components/conversion-details.tsx:401
msgid "Yes. Units Converters is free to use for students, professionals, and everyday tasks. Results are provided for informational purposes—always follow your industry standards for safety-critical work."
msgstr "Ya. Units Converters gratis digunakan untuk pelajar, profesional, dan tugas sehari-hari. Hasil diberikan untuk tujuan informasi—selalu ikuti standar industri Anda untuk pekerjaan yang mengutamakan keselamatan."

#: src/lib/units.ts:1224
msgid "Yoctometre"
msgstr "Yoktometer"

#: src/lib/units.ts:1229
msgid "Yottametre"
msgstr "Yottameter"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1623
msgid "You almost always pay on the greater of actual weight and dimensional weight. A box of pillows can be light on the scale and expensive on the invoice because volume weight wins. A small dense part can be heavy and tiny—actual weight wins. Unit conversion mistakes on either side change which number wins."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:173
msgid "You always multiply by a ratio equal to one. Whether the numerical factor looks like multiplication or division depends on which way you write the ratio. If the unit you want to eliminate is in the denominator of your measurement, put it in the numerator of the factor so it cancels."
msgstr "Anda selalu mengalikannya dengan rasio yang sama dengan satu. Apakah faktor numerik terlihat seperti perkalian atau pembagian bergantung pada cara Anda menulis rasio. Jika satuan yang ingin dihilangkan ada pada penyebut hasil pengukuran, masukkan ke dalam pembilang faktor sehingga hilang."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1126
msgid "You cannot verify a 20 nm feature with a kitchen ruler. Match the instrument to the scale: electron microscopy and specialised metrology for nanometres; optical microscopy for micrometres; micrometers and CMMs for millimetres. Conversion cannot upgrade an instrument’s resolution."
msgstr "Anda tidak dapat memverifikasi fitur 20 nm dengan penggaris dapur. Cocokkan instrumen dengan skala: mikroskop elektron dan metrologi khusus untuk nanometer; mikroskop optik untuk mikrometer; mikrometer dan CMM untuk milimeter. Konversi tidak dapat meningkatkan resolusi instrumen."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:628
msgid "You may have multiplied by 0.3048 once instead of by 0.3048 squared (about 0.0929). Area conversions must square the length factor."
msgstr "Anda mungkin mengalikannya dengan 0,3048 satu kali, bukan dengan 0,3048 kuadrat (sekitar 0,0929). Konversi luas harus mengkuadratkan faktor panjang."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1525
msgid "You need three length measurements (or an equivalent geometry) to get volume, then convert that volume to the chemical chart’s unit."
msgstr "Anda memerlukan tiga pengukuran panjang (atau geometri yang setara) untuk mendapatkan volume, lalu mengonversi volume tersebut ke satuan grafik kimia."

#: src/routes/$lang/privacy-policy.tsx:267
msgid "Your rights"
msgstr "Hak Anda"

#: src/lib/units.ts:1225
msgid "Zeptometre"
msgstr "Zeptometer"

#: src/lib/units.ts:1226
msgid "Zettametre"
msgstr "Zettameter"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:834
msgid "Zoning documents sometimes switch units between sections. Create a one-page unit key for the project and convert every cited figure into a single working unit."
msgstr "Dokumen zonasi terkadang berpindah unit antar bagian. Buat kunci unit satu halaman untuk proyek tersebut dan ubah setiap angka yang dikutip menjadi satu unit kerja."
